'''Warner Bros.,''' officially '''Warner Bros. Entertainment Inc.,''' is an American entertainment company. It was originally founded in [[1920s|1923]] by brothers [[Wikipedia:Jack L. Warner|Jack]], [[Wikipedia:Harry Warner|Harry]], [[Wikipedia:Albert Warner|Albert]] and [[Wikipedia:Sam Warner|Sam Warner]].

==Relationship with Lucasfilm==
Warner Bros. is part of [[Wikipedia:WarnerMedia|WarnerMedia]] which encompasses [[Cartoon Network]] and [[Turner Network Television]], which both aired the ''[[Star Wars: The Clone Wars]]'' television series. Prior to the release of the series, Warner Bros. distributed the [[Star Wars: The Clone Wars (film)|''Star Wars: The Clone Wars'']] film, marking the first time that a U.S. theatrical ''[[Star Wars]]'' film was not distributed by [[20th Century Studios|20th Century Fox]], which distributed all six films in the main ''Star Wars'' saga before [[Lucasfilm]] was acquired by the [[The Walt Disney Company]] in [[2012]].

Warner Bros. also owns [[Warner Bros. Interactive Entertainment]], which is owns [[Traveller's Tales]] and [[TT Games]], the studios behind the ''[[LEGO Star Wars]]'' [[Star Wars video games|video games]].

Before ''Star Wars: The Clone Wars'', Warner Bros. also distributed [[George Lucas]]' [[1971]] film, [[Wikipedia:THX 1138|''THX 1138'']].

